                : "TA-Lib computes (high-close)/((high-low)/-100), returns zero on a flat or underflowed denominator, and requires period >=2. WilliamsR returns -100 on a flat range and evaluates the complete ratio exactly before rounding, preserving finite results across oversized or subnormal ranges. Native flat, underflow, overflow, and period boundaries have executable regressions and a separate staged reference. One-bar input is rejected by the native range validator.";
        if (api.Id == "Trady.Indicator.HighestHighLowestLowDifference")
