                : "Trady defaults to cumulative typical-price VWAP and also supports a nullable rolling period; both modes, object/tuple routes, and full-window startup are verified. Native decimal arithmetic rounds typical price before weighting, throws on zero total volume or nonpositive periods, and can overflow products before a finite result. VolumeWeightedPrice retains the complete exact weighted ratio, reports zero total volume as absent, and requires positive rolling periods. Independent references and direct exception regressions pin the differences.";
